{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/OPENING-CENSUS.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/opening_census.py; rg -n '\"'^## D(248|187|665|382|685)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Phase 2, step 1: why the old system never opens 16 of the 32 matters ($0, D685)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Source:** `opening_census.py`, written to `poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/opening-census.json`. For each matter's articles in each old\n     4\tdraw it records:\n     5\t- the candidate questions the extraction proposed, and what matching did with each;\n     6\t- where the evidence from those articles was linked;\n     7\t- the mapping readers' verdict (`reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L*-*.txt`).\n     8\t\n     9\tClaude read every row.\n    10\t\n    11\t## The answer\n    12\tNone of the 16 is lost because the old system failed to see the facts. In every draw it wrote evidence from those articles, between 2\n    13\tand 138 items a matter, and linked most of it to questions it holds. There are three causes, and **two of them are design rules Alex\n    14\tset.**\n    15\t\n    16\t| Cause | Matters | What happens | Rule behind it |\n    17\t|---|---|---|---|\n    18\t| **A. One bet, one question.** The scoring list splits a bet that the system keeps as one question | M02, M03, M24 (five-company capex, total and data-center), M26, M28 (the EU and U.S. review stages of the Hugging Face deal), M27 (the Hugging Face obligation amount), M12 (the Ohio lease-guarantee amount), M20 ($125B residual-value support), M32 (neocloud capacity commitments), M07 (FY2028 data-center revenue) | The extraction proposes the variant, and matching merges it into the held question. old-1 proposed \"top five hyperscalers' capex\" 8 times; each merged into the four-company question. Otherwise the variant's evidence goes to the held question: the Ohio guarantee's to \"will NVIDIA sign the guarantee\", the $125B's and the capacity commitments' to \"credit support, guarantees and capacity backstops\", FY2028 data-center revenue's to FY2028 total revenue. The mapping readers mark these \"broader\" or \"missed\": old-2 Q43 joins the U.S. and EU clearances by 2027-06-30, and the list asks for each review stage at 2027-01-31 | D248, \"one bet, one question\" (Alex). The comparison's frozen matter list (D671) is finer than D248 for these 10 |\n    19\t| **B. The library's subject is NVIDIA only** | M01, M22 (Broadcom's AI revenue, FY2027 and FY2026), M23 (CoreWeave's revenue), M29 (Marvell's revenue), M21 (Alphabet's capex) | Every request says \"[Subjects] The objects this item concerns: NVDA\". The prompt puts a company's own figure under that company's ticker. The old draws proposed 0 candidates with any company object other than NVDA. The evidence went to NVIDIA's revenue questions | The corpus tags NVDA as the only subject. Broadcom, CoreWeave and Alphabet are on the research list (`poc/universe.json`); Marvell is not. D187: a company's own quantity is a thesis under that company |\n    20\t| **C. A theme proposed under the wrong name, or not proposed** | M16 (DRAM prices in 2027); M05 (2026 semiconductor sales, served in 1 of 3 draws) | M05: old-2 proposed it under the object \"Semiconductor sales worldwide\", and the research-list check refused it. old-3 used `semiconductor-cycle` and opened it. old-1 did not propose it. M16 was proposed in no draw | Within the standing decisions |\n    21\t\n    22\t## The attainable ceiling (council K's falsifier)\n    23\t- **Within the standing decisions:**\n    24\t  - the judge, +2 (M08 and M14), not reached by any tested change;\n    25\t  - cause C, up to +2 (M05 steadied, M16);\n    26\t  - the matters served in only 1 of 3 draws (M09, M25, M30), whose share is uncertain.\n    27\t\n    28\t  **That is about 4 to 6 at best, every piece uncertain, against D665's lead of 5.** The hybrid cannot be shown better than old\n    29\t  without one of Alex's rules changing.\n    30\t- **The generous ceiling:** if cause A were opened as separate questions (+10) or cause B's companies were tagged (+5), it is well\n    31\t  above 5. So the falsifier does not fire as worded. **The constraints that set the ceiling are D248 and the library's NVIDIA-only\n    32\t  subject, both Alex's**, together with D382 (company figures: 7 of the 32 are company figures, and old serves 5 or 6 of them).\n    33\t- **The concern is recorded, as D373 requires, and the frozen list is not changed.** For cause A, the comparison's matter list is\n    34\t  finer than D248. Splitting five-company from four-company capex, or the EU stage of a review from the U.S. stage, is the\n    35\t  \"wordings, deadlines, milestones and periods of one bet\" that D248 keeps as one question.\n     1\t\"\"\"Phase 2, step 1 (D685): where each of the 32 frozen matters falls out of the old system's opening, per old draw ($0, read-only).\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 opening_census.py            # writes poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/opening-census.json and prints one block per matter\n     4\t\n     5\tFor each matter and old draw, from the matter's articles (the frozen census numbering): the candidate questions the extraction proposed\n     6\tfrom those articles and what matching did with each (opened new, merged into an existing question, succession, or not opened with its\n     7\treason, or refused by a check), the evidence written from those articles and the questions it was linked to, and the evidence dropped\n     8\twith no home. The mapping's verdict (which old question covers the matter) is printed beside it.\"\"\"\n     9\timport json\n    10\timport sys\n    11\tfrom collections import Counter\n    12\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    13\t\n    14\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    15\tsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\n    16\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    17\timport judge_probe as jp  # noqa: E402\n    18\t\n    19\tCENSUS = jp.ROOT / 'docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census'\n    20\tMAPPING = jp.DIAG / 'mapping-out/mapping.json'\n    21\tOLD = ('old-1', 'old-2', 'old-3')\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\tdef trace(draw, inputs):\n    25\t    views, _ = jp.store_paths(draw)\n    26\t    conn = jp.readonly(views)\n    27\t    question = {r['view_id']: r['question'] for r in conn.execute('select view_id, question from views')}\n    28\t    out = {'candidates': [], 'linked': Counter(), 'no_home': 0, 'evidence': 0}\n    29\t    for input_id in inputs:\n    30\t        handover = conn.execute('select handover_json from handovers where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone()\n    31\t        if handover is None:\n    32\t            out.setdefault('not_handed_over', []).append(input_id)\n    33\t            continue\n    34\t        h = json.loads(handover[0])\n    35\t        out['evidence'] += len(h['evidence'])\n    36\t        out['no_home'] += sum(1 for d in h['dropped'] if d[1] == 'no home')\n    37\t        decided = {}\n    38\t        for r in conn.execute('select decisions_json, checks_json from match_records where input_id=? order by call_no', (input_id,)):\n    39\t            d = json.loads(r['decisions_json']) if r['decisions_json'] else {}\n    40\t            checks = json.loads(r['checks_json']) if r['checks_json'] else {}\n    41\t            for c in d.get('candidates', []):\n    42\t                decided[c['id']] = {'outcome': c.get('outcome'), 'target': c.get('target_view_id'), 'reason': c.get('reason', '')[:160]}\n    43\t            for cid, why in (checks.get('not_opened') or {}).items():\n    44\t                decided.setdefault(cid, {})['not_opened'] = why\n    45\t            for refusal in checks.get('refusals') or []:\n    46\t                cid = refusal.split(':', 1)[0].replace('candidate ', '').strip()\n    47\t                decided.setdefault(cid, {})['refused'] = refusal[:200]\n    48\t        for c in h['candidates']:\n    49\t            fate = decided.get(c['id'], {'outcome': 'no match record'})\n    50\t            target = fate.get('target')\n    51\t            out['candidates'].append({'input': input_id, 'object': c['object'], 'kind': c['kind'], 'question': c['question'],\n    52\t                                      'fate': fate, 'target_question': question.get(target) if target else None})\n    53\t        for r in conn.execute('select distinct l.view_id from evidence_sources s join evidence_links l on l.evidence_id = s.evidence_id '\n    54\t                              'where s.input_id=?', (input_id,)):\n    55\t            out['linked'][question.get(r['view_id'], r['view_id'])] += 1\n    56\t    out['linked'] = dict(out['linked'].most_common(8))\n    57\t    return out\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\tdef main():\n    61\t    matters = json.loads((CENSUS / 'matters.json').read_text())['matters']\n    62\t    numbering = json.loads((CENSUS / 'numbering.json').read_text())\n    63\t    mapping = json.loads(MAPPING.read_text())['mapping']\n    64\t    report = []\n    65\t    for m in matters:\n    66\t        inputs = [numbering[str(k)] for k in m['articles']]\n    67\t        covered = {d: mapping.get(d, {}).get(m['matter'], []) for d in OLD}\n    68\t        row = {'matter': m['matter'], 'name': m['name'], 'question': m['question'], 'company_figure': m['company_figure'],\n    69\t               'articles': len(inputs), 'covered_by': covered, 'draws': {d: trace(d, inputs) for d in OLD}}\n    70\t        report.append(row)\n    71\t        print(f\"\\n=== {m['matter']} {'[company figure] ' if m['company_figure'] else ''}{m['name']} | {len(inputs)} articles | covered: \"\n    72\t              + '; '.join(f\"{d}: {[q['question'] + ('' if q['covers'] is True else ' (' + str(q['covers']) + ')') for q in qs]}\" for d, qs in covered.items()))\n    73\t        for d, t in row['draws'].items():\n    74\t            print(f\"  {d}: evidence {t['evidence']}, no home {t['no_home']}, candidates {len(t['candidates'])}\")\n    75\t            for c in t['candidates']:\n    76\t                f = c['fate']\n    77\t                print(f\"    - [{c['object']}/{c['kind']}] {c['question'][:110]} -> {f.get('outcome')}\"\n    78\t                      + (f\" into: {c['target_question'][:80]}\" if c['target_question'] else '')\n    79\t                      + (f\" | NOT OPENED: {f['not_opened'][:90]}\" if f.get('not_opened') else '') + (f\" | REFUSED: {f['refused'][:90]}\" if f.get('refused') else ''))\n    80\t            if not t['candidates']:\n    81\t                print(f\"    linked to: {list(t['linked'].items())[:4]}\")\n    82\t    (jp.OUT / 'opening-census.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    86\t    main()\n2480:## D187 · 2026-10-26 · A company's own quantity sits under that company's object, private companies included\n2954:## D248 · 2026-10-30 · What counts as one question and one piece of evidence: seven boundaries, chosen one by one\n4107:## D382 · 2026-11-08 · Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason\n9398:## D665 · 2026-11-17 · Council (D664, Alex's \"run your council to determine\"): the six lines stop blocking release; one product comparison against the running pipeline decides readiness, its verdict written before the first send (council consensus)\n10212:## D685 · 2026-11-20 · Under D684 (councils I–K): the fresh test cannot be fed; H1 fails its diagnostic; the judge line pauses within D198; phase 2 (opening) starts\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat poc/universe.json; python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib; base=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/opening-census.json\\\"); a=json.loads(base.read_text()); print(type(a),len(a)); print(list(a) if isinstance(a,dict) else a[0]); b=json.loads(pathlib.Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json\\\").read_text()); print(type(b),len(b)); print(list(b) if isinstance(b,dict) else b[0]);'; wc -l poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L*-{claude,codex}.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat poc/universe.json; python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib; base=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/opening-census.json\\\"); a=json.loads(base.read_text()); print(type(a),len(a)); print(list(a) if isinstance(a,dict) else a[0]); b=json.loads(pathlib.Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json\\\").read_text()); print(type(b),len(b)); print(list(b) if isinstance(b,dict) else b[0]);'; wc -l poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L*-{claude,codex}.txt\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"version\": \"poc-2026-10-25-en1\",\n \"_note\": \"The research list for the POC (01-universe.md): which objects, and which categories each is watched in. Items in the corpus carry object labels from the upstream feed; only objects listed here can have views opened. Each object carries `watch`, the analyst's reference list of quantities {measure, scope?, event_type?} (D155: a reference shown to the model, not a gate). 2026-10-25 (D163): theme names in English; the former Chinese names are aliases and `legacy_name`, which the Chinese prompt versions (up to v5) print so that their stored requests stay byte-identical.\",\n \"companies\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NVDA\",\n   \"name\": \"NVIDIA\",\n   \"categories\": [\n    \"T1\",\n    \"T2\",\n    \"T3\",\n    \"T4\",\n    \"T5\",\n    \"T6\",\n    \"T7\",\n    \"T8\",\n    \"T9\",\n    \"T10\"\n   ],\n   \"fiscal_year_end_month\": 1,\n   \"aliases\": [\n    \"NVIDIA\",\n    \"Nvidia\",\n    \"英伟达\",\n    \"辉达\",\n    \"Blackwell\",\n    \"Rubin\",\n    \"Vera Rubin\",\n    \"Vera\",\n    \"Hopper\",\n    \"H100\",\n    \"H200\",\n    \"H20\",\n    \"B200\",\n    \"B300\",\n    \"GB200\",\n    \"GB300\",\n    \"NVL72\",\n    \"DGX\",\n    \"DGX Spark\",\n    \"GeForce\",\n    \"GeForce NOW\",\n    \"RTX\",\n    \"CUDA\",\n    \"NVLink\",\n    \"Jensen Huang\",\n    \"黄仁勋\",\n    \"Grace\"\n   ],\n   \"watch\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"total_revenue\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"segment_revenue\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"gross_margin\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"operating_margin\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"operating_expense_growth\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"tax_rate\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"capex\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"product_revenue\",\n     \"scope\": \"Blackwell+Rubin\",\n     \"aliases\": [\n      \"blackwell\",\n      \"rubin\",\n      \"blackwell and rubin\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"product_revenue\",\n     \"scope\": \"Vera\",\n     \"aliases\": [\n      \"vera cpu\",\n      \"vera standalone\",\n      \"vera\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"shipments_or_capacity\",\n     \"scope\": \"Rubin\",\n     \"aliases\": [\n      \"rubin\",\n      \"vera rubin\",\n      \"nvl72\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"event\",\n     \"event_type\": \"shipment\",\n     \"scope\": \"Rubin\",\n     \"aliases\": [\n      \"rubin\",\n      \"vera rubin\",\n      \"nvl72\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"event\",\n     \"event_type\": \"launch\",\n     \"scope\": \"Rubin\",\n     \"aliases\": [\n      \"rubin\",\n      \"vera rubin\",\n      \"nvl72\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"event\",\n     \"event_type\": \"licence\",\n     \"scope\": \"H20/H200 China\",\n     \"aliases\": [\n      \"h20\",\n      \"h200\",\n      \"china licence\",\n      \"china license\",\n      \"export licen\",\n      \"对华\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"event\",\n     \"event_type\": \"deployment\",\n     \"scope\": \"SK Telecom AI factory\",\n     \"aliases\": [\n      \"sk telecom\",\n      \"sk group\",\n      \"sk ai\"\n     ]\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"TSM\",\n   \"name\": \"Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing\",\n   \"categories\": [\n    \"T1\",\n    \"T2\",\n    \"T4\",\n    \"T6\",\n  