{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '2480,2492p;2954,2977p;4107,4120p;9398,9442p;10212,10248p'; rg -n '\\\"id\\\": \\\"(AVGO|CRWV|GOOGL|GOOG|MRVL|semiconductor-cycle)\\\"|DRAM|Marvell' poc/universe.json\"","aggregated_output":"  2480\t## D187 · 2026-10-26 · A company's own quantity sits under that company's object, private companies included\n  2481\t\n  2482\t- Alex chose option C (\"可以\"): any company's own quantity is a thesis under that company (SpaceX's compute capacity under SpaceX, Alphabet's capital spending under GOOGL), consistent with 06-views rule 5 (\"company figures use the fiscal year\"); a macro theme opens only when a thesis depends on it. Recorded; not implemented in this slice: it needs a private-company object kind in the universe and the one switch (01-universe), its own slice. Until then the gold accepts the Codex reading (evidence to NVDA data-center revenue) for SpaceX.\n  2483\t\n  2484\t## D188 · 2026-10-26 · The extraction gold: twenty cases labelled by the assistant this round, human review later\n  2485\t\n  2486\t- Alex: \"不是你要标吗？之后我们可以human in the loop, but this time in the beginning just use the research you just did\"; \"标20条\". The gold `poc/eval/gold/extraction-admission-2026-10-26.json` holds 20 cases from the real items (the report §5's 15 plus five: CoreWeave managed-inference ARR, the four-company $745bn figure, the Bloomberg NAVER retelling, the Taiwan smuggling clause, the Goldman 2027 aggregate), each with the theses that must open (typed keys: object, measure, year, event type, scope pattern, with acceptable alternatives), the theses that must not open, the evidence links that must exist and the baseline's score. Scoring (`scripts/score_admission_gold.py`): fail when a must-open thesis or an evidence target is missing; partial when all are present but a must-not-open thesis was created; full otherwise; \"not processed\" when the run never saw the item. Labelled `assistant`; a human pass with two labellers and a reported agreement is the next protocol step, not this one.\n  2487\t\n  2488\t## D189 · 2026-10-26 · poc-v25 is the replay default; the trace review names the next mechanisms\n  2489\t\n  2490\t- Alex, after the measurement: \"你可以取代，但是看所有的 trace 然后告诉我我们怎么持续做的更好接近 golden … We don't want to overfit … It needs to act exactly like a very senior hedge fund analyst\". `scripts/replay.py` now defaults to `poc/config/poc-v25.json` (extraction v12, Jev matching); `poc-v23` stays as a configuration and replays unchanged.\n  2491\t- The [trace review](research/2026-10-26-thesis-admission-v12/trace-review.md) reads every thesis, every gold failure and the duplicate aggregates to their raw requests, answers and matching decisions, and names the root causes by design layer: thesis identity is a quantity where the analyst's unit is a question (six 2026 aggregates, each judged \"new\" correctly under the current criterion); the contract under-produces on first contact with a company (AMD 2 theses, MSFT 0); the role states categories where the labeller applies tests; theme candidates name no dependant; the extractor never sees the current view. Six general mechanisms are proposed with the class and count each moves, in the order: matching's \"another estimate or population of the same question\" option and theme dependants (code and schema, no prompt growth), then role v13 (tests instead of lists, the first-contact rule, quarterly statements as evidence; net shorter), then showing the view in block 5 as an A/B, then the daily duplicate check as pull-mode design. Each is Alex's call; none is built here.\n  2492\t\n  2954\t## D248 · 2026-10-30 · What counts as one question and one piece of evidence: seven boundaries, chosen one by one\n  2955\t\n  2956\t- Alex, on the census of duplicate and trivial questions: \"我们的标准要收口\"; then \"你要不要深度的写好plan, 怎么测量，golden 是怎么，我们来解决这个问题；整体不能regress，你要秉持我们过往工程的原则，以及作为一个hedge fund analyst 到底怎么判断合并，去重，这个标准很重要，不能观点爆炸\"; then, not following the plan's table, \"我没理解每个难点，我需要一个一个和你过，你讲人话给我例子\". Each boundary was put to him with an example and two options; his replies are quoted per row. Plan, census and review rounds: [question-identity plan](research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md) §0–§4, §11b, §12.\n  2957\t- The class ($0, `census/`): the sealed three-month run opened 69 questions in 59 days; Claude's reading of the first 50 (not reviewed by Alex) marks 12 duplicates and 10 that should not have opened, 5 borderline. Matching merged 39 of 122 candidates; the candidates opened new fall in three verdict classes (parsed from the decisions' reason text, not yet verified case by case): the collision judge's \"distinct question in one matter\", \"same question\" verdicts the code still opened (two traced to a model-written period start), and twins never compared.\n  2958\t- The principle, Alex after the seven answers: \"我觉得核心就是这个颗粒度的把控要符合一个高端的hedge fund analyst 的思维。不要搜集一堆鸡毛蒜皮的事情，要看重要的大事，合并整合关键的信息，这个是这个步骤的原则\" (written into AGENTS §8, \"A senior analyst's granularity\").\n  2959\t- Decided (the general rule under all seven: two questions are one when the same outcome settles both; they are kept apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on each separately):\n  2960\t  1. **One plan, several wordings** (H1, \"A\"): wordings of one plan whose final check is the same number are one question; two numbers that move on their own and are watched separately stay apart; a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it. Not put to Alex: a not-yet-signed deal's yes/no signing question (D210; PRD 06 keeps number and event questions apart) stays as it is and does not merge into a plan's amount question (the Ohio lease guarantee and the cloud-customer total in v38 both stay). Narrows the standard §4 \"another quantity in the same deal (a guarantee beside a financing)\" sentence taken from D190; consistent with D210.\n  2961\t  2. **One event, several deadlines** (H2, \"A\"): while the earlier-deadline question is open, a later deadline is its evidence, not a new question; when the earlier one falls due unresolved and the matter is still live, the system opens the next-deadline successor with the merged evidence, without waiting for a new article (new work for pull mode, D14, D54).\n  2962\t  3. **One product generation, several milestones** (H3, \"A\"): one question per generation, asked at the step that brings revenue (shipments begin); sampling and launch are its evidence; only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's phase-3 data and its approval) are separate questions.\n  2963\t  4. **A company's own quantity by fiscal and by calendar year** (H4, \"A\"): only the fiscal year opens (PRD 06 ladder rule 5); a calendar-year estimate is evidence to the fiscal question, weighed lower when the years differ much.\n  2964\t  5. **A model-written period start** (H5, \"A\"): for event and policy questions it no longer blocks a merge; object, event and due day are still checked.\n  2965\t  6. **Small matters opened as questions** (H6, \"A， A\"): a deal, product or project (the question was put about small deals and products) opens a question only when its scale can change the company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk; otherwise no question opens, and whether its statement is kept follows the evidence rule (standard §5). Done in this round together with the merge changes, each measured as its own arm, then together on the holdout. Narrows the standard §3 class C (\"a sized, not yet completed stake or acquisition\").\n  2966\t  7. **The same statement carried by several outlets** (H7, \"A\"): code treats pieces with the same known original speaker, original day and figures as one (an unknown speaker or day never matches: 297 of the sealed run's 4,298 pieces have both unknown); the judge sees it once with the outlet count; every piece is still stored. Changes D204's \"both shown to the judge\" for this case, and is a chosen exception to AGENTS §3 \"equal values alone never establish identity\"; the risk put to him with the question (a qualification such as \"excluding China sales\" hidden; D204's 8 of 40 wrong merges) is measured on the G3 gold before it is switched on, as is the accuracy of the original-speaker and original-day fields it relies on.\n  2967\t- Next, in this order: the signed standard page (§3 class C, §4 \"same question, succession or another question\") carries these rules, then a read-only Codex drift review; then the plan's step 1 (structured census, the fixed-extraction replay harness, gold G1–G3, the September holdout week on Alex's go).\n  2968\t\n  2969\t## D249 · 2026-10-30 · A test the model applies to each statement is a check at the end of the same request; role-v63 (`poc-v79`) measured, the default stays role-v53\n  2970\t\n  2971\t- Alex, after a second-turn probe judged statements by standard 5.1 correctly that the one-pass answer had kept: \"那为什么你不在prompt 里面要求做完自己复核一边就好，这样就是一个call完成\"; then \"你尝试一组先吧，这个完全就是再prompt 的最后面要求做完一遍基于\"你刚才说的复核条件\"再跑一次；写在同一个提示词里面\"; then \"可以，但是这个做法是有效的对吧，那你应该好好地写复核的侧重点然后跑；这个如果有效可以记录下来这个做法\"; then the goal \"你需要让这个加到prompt里面的方式improve performance. 一定要improve but don't hardcode or break our principles\".\n  2972\t- Decided (the method, written at AGENTS §6): from role-v59 the extraction request ends with a check that reads the evidence list back by standard 5.1 (`prompts/review-v<N>.txt`, `extraction.REVIEW_FROM`) and names no empty-answer condition; the role text of role-v59 to role-v63 is role-v53's. Every line of the check cites the standard (§5.1, §5.3, §6, D238, D243, D240); six read-only Codex rounds (`research/2026-10-30-noise/codex-review-*`); examples from other industries.\n  2973\t- Measured (run Y3, role-v53 and role-v63 sent together, development 118 + test 30 articles, three draws; `loop-log.md` rows 34–48): gold-rejected statements kept per draw 94.3 → 77.3 (−17, interval −33 to −2); core kept in every draw 72 → 74 of 86 and supporting in at least two draws 152 → 154 of 181 once a blind reader judged the 58 entries the counting aid scored differently (core draws 31 → 34, supporting 85 → 85); test supporting in at least two draws 38 → 41 of 42.\n  2974\t- Not decided: switching the default to `poc-v79`. Alex's reply to the report was \"你可以commit push\", with further noise work asked (\"但是还是有70多篇被留下\"), not an answer to the switch; `scripts/replay.py` stays on `poc-v69`.\n  2975\t\n  2976\t## D250 · 2026-10-31 · Four evidence boundaries and the counting unit settled; the ruler is fixed before any further measurement (standard version 5)\n  2977\t\n  4107\t## D382 · 2026-11-08 · Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason\n  4108\t\n  4109\t- Alex: \"我觉得财务类型不应该是thesis，而更多的是条件。观点应该是独特的view，而不是喊出来的数字，除非有理由 - 这个理由恰恰才是观点\". On the\n  4110\t  recommendation to keep a useful company figure no view takes as a condition of the company, he replied \"好\". Record:\n  4111\t  `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §§16–17.\n  4112\t\n  4113\t## D383 · 2026-11-08 · D209 amended again: a material statement no thesis takes is kept unlinked and linked later\n  4114\t\n  4115\t- Alex chose \"先存着，有观点再挂\": a statement the model judges useful but no thesis takes yet is kept in the company's record, linked when\n  4116\t  a related thesis opens; what the closing check rejects is still dropped, including the cash flow he ruled out. Amends D209 beyond D382.\n  4117\t  Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §27.\n  4118\t\n  4119\t## D384 · 2026-11-08 · Clean Step 1 opens only the big matters, by the signed standard as the frozen gold applies it\n  4120\t\n  9398\t## D665 · 2026-11-17 · Council (D664, Alex's \"run your council to determine\"): the six lines stop blocking release; one product comparison against the running pipeline decides readiness, its verdict written before the first send (council consensus)\n  9399\t\n  9400\t- **Council** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-10/`):\n  9401\t  - Claude's own position, written first (`own-position.md`);\n  9402\t  - the Codex reading (`codex-1.md`, thread 01a1ebfe-4f67-7c72-af87-7830055e0f09, memories off);\n  9403\t  - the Claude-family reading (`claude-1.md`);\n  9404\t  - challenge rounds (`codex-2.md`: disagree, four corrections; `codex-3.md`: \"CONSENSUS\", with one sentence added).\n  9405\t- **Why the six lines stop blocking:**\n  9406\t  - D400 wrote them for \"this first measurement\" and told Alex they \"不能证明它比老系统好\". D548, a council decision, made them gate 1.\n  9407\t  - D560 found no measured link between them and the final answer.\n  9408\t  - Their zero-fault forms are a poor target at the measured luna-era rates (D623): zero faults in 131 sends has even odds only near 0.5% a send.\n  9409\t  - Reader agreement on disputed points is 21 of 70 and 29 of 53, and draws move from 7 failures to 1 (D650).\n  9410\t- **Decided:** as written in `clean-arch/PRD.md` §1.5, which now owns the rule.\n  9411\t  1. **The product comparison is the release decision.**\n  9412\t     - poc-v118 is replayed against the hashed new system (astra-frozen; v5.5 excluded). Both start from empty over 07-01 to 07-19, three draws\n  9413\t       each, and are scored on unread weeks from 07-20 up to 09-20, as far as the full exposure census supports. The exclusion list is frozen.\n  9414\t     - **The main quantity:** big matters served, paired per matter.\n  9415\t     - **Verdicts:**\n  9416\t       - **Practical lead:** a − b ≥ max(3, 15% of N) and a ≥ 2b. Every guardrail subgroup must meet its frozen minimum and pass under both split\n  9417\t         countings.\n  9418\t       - **Practical loss:** the mirror, or a guardrail breach confirmed under both countings.\n  9419\t       - **No practical winner, too small or invalid**, as written.\n  9420\t     - **Guardrails:** unsupported shares (figure and yes/no apart) and the not-worth-tracking share, each within 10 points of the old system's.\n  9421\t       D428's limits are printed beside them.\n  9422\t     - **Illustrative only:** a sign test and an interval.\n  9423\t     - **Frozen and hashed before the first send:** the matter list (blind), the credit rules (one cutoff per matter, the grouping of repeats,\n  9424\t       what counts as the same question), the controls, the versions and the rule.\n  9425\t  2. **What changes, explicitly:**\n  9426\t     - D548's use of D400's six lines as a release gate is superseded. The lines are reported on every ladder run.\n  9427\t     - The parts code decides stay hard: figure ranges meet end to end; the favourable end is stable; the due day is consistent at D400's 90%.\n  9428\t     - D431's frozen-reference reading of 07-01 to 07-14 is still produced and printed beside the comparison, not deciding. D665 supersedes D431\n  9429\t       on that point only.\n  9430\t     - Step 2's three checks stay as D427 and D431 set them.\n  9431\t     - Gate 2's unsupported lines become the guardrails, and its control line waits (D658).\n  9432\t     - Gate 4 folds in.\n  9433\t     - Gate 5 waits for a practical lead and Alex's word.\n  9434\t     - The absolute floors stay proposals, reported beside.\n  9435\t  3. **Back to Alex,** before any release engineering resumes: a practical lead (with the split cards for his spot check), a practical loss at\n  9436\t     once, no practical winner, too small or invalid, or no verdict by 2026-12-01.\n  9437\t- **Next:**\n  9438\t  - the comparison's design at $0: the exposure census, the frozen matter list and credit rules, the cards and controls, the replay plan and\n  9439\t    its spend guard;\n  9440\t  - council review;\n  9441\t  - then a send on Alex's word. No budget is required (D664).\n  9442\t\n 10212\t## D685 · 2026-11-20 · Under D684 (councils I–K): the fresh test cannot be fed; H1 fails its diagnostic; the judge line pauses within D198; phase 2 (opening) starts\n 10213\t\n 10214\t- **The fresh census** (`DESIGN-J2.md`, \"The fresh census and council J\"): 116 answers as of 09-06, read blind by both families.\n 10215\t  - Once the bets the design had read were excluded (council I), 27 fresh bets gave 1 target against the 8 required. The selection\n 10216\t    refused itself, and nothing was sent.\n 10217\t  - On this corpus, the judge's errors sit in about ten big numeric bets, all of which the design has read.\n 10218\t- **H1** (the heading only, council H's recommendation) was tested in council J's diagnostic: three motivating targets, two controls,\n 10219\t  3 repeats against same-day v7, 32 cards blind-read with 2 plants.\n 10220\t  - Result: **0 net repairs against 2 required.** No control was lost, no refusals, and both plants were caught. **H1 is retired.**\n 10221\t  - By code, it kept the rejected rung in 8 of 9 target answers. The carried derivation, not its label, holds the rung.\n 10222\t  - Spend: $0.08 from `phase1b`, which now stands at $0.36 of $2.\n 10223\t- **Reflection council K** (a cold read, consensus with Claude's reflection apart from one point):\n 10224\t  - Four angles on the judge have failed. Every remaining lever changes D198.\n 10225\t  - The judge's ceiling on the 32 matters is M08 and M14.\n 10226\t  - **Decided:**\n 10227\t    - D198 stays in place, and its options are not taken to Alex yet;\n 10228\t    - **phase 2 starts**: a $0 census of the 17 matters old never opened (where each fell out, and whether the evidence then available\n 10229\t      could support an answer), and the attainable gain under each company-figure policy (D382 open);\n 10230\t    - **falsifier:** if even the generous ceiling, the two judge repairs included, is below 5 more matters, the plan changes to address\n 10231\t      the constraint that sets that ceiling. Otherwise the strongest opening fix is tested on final answers against D665's line:\n 10232\t      5 net gains, and at least twice as many wins as losses.\n 10233\t  - Claude's reflection had proposed taking D198's options to Alex now. Council K: not before the census shows what the hybrid can\n 10234\t    gain. Claude agrees.\n 10235\t- **Errors of mine:**\n 10236\t  - I read 7% at 09-06 against 17% at 09-20 as \"errors accumulate\". The two pools are chosen differently, so this is withdrawn\n 10237\t    (council J).\n 10238\t  - The first fresh pool held questions the design had read in other draws (council I).\n274:   \"id\": \"AVGO\",\n478:   \"id\": \"GOOGL\",\n647:   \"id\": \"CRWV\",\n925:   \"id\": \"semiconductor-cycle\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib; q=pathlib.Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json\\\"); w=json.loads(q.read_text()); print({k:v for k,v in w.items() if k\"'!=\"matters\"});\nfor m in w[\"matters\"]: print(m[\"matter\"],m[\"company_figure\"],m[\"name\"],m[\"question\"],m[\"articles\"])'\"'; rg -n '\"'^M(0[1-9]|1[2-8]|2[0-9]|3[02])'\"\\\\b|M0[2357]|M1[26]|M2[04678]|M32' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L{1,2,6}-{claude,codex}.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib; q=pathlib.Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json\\\"); w=json.loads(q.read_text()); print({k:v for k,v in w.items() if k\"'!=\"matters\"});\nfor m in w[\"matters\"]: print(m[\"matter\"],m[\"company_figure\"],m[\"name\"],m[\"question\"],m[\"articles\"])'\"'; rg -n '\"'^M(0[1-9]|1[2-8]|2[0-9]|3[02])'\"\\\\b|M0[2357]|M1[26]|M2[04678]|M32' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L{1,2,6}-{claude,codex}.txt\"","aggregated_output":"{'frozen': 'stage 0, before any system output (D671)', 'entries_sha256': '4cb55c547ddad2f4f3bf40c561bcb423eda382a8ff01f062263fcb1cb5d32d17', 'rule': 'one matter per group of entries joined by a grouping both families made or a pair both blind adjudicators read as one bet (D248)', 'N': 32, 'company_figure_subgroup': 7, 'adjudicated_one_bet': [[3, 27]], 'adjudication_splits': {'2-26': {'codex': False, 'claude': True}, '12-37': {'codex': False, 'claude': True}}}\nM01 False Broadcom FY2027 AI semiconductor revenue What will Broadcom's AI semiconductor revenue be in FY2027? [6, 14, 123, 130, 144, 203, 317, 343, 366]\nM02 False Five major hyperscalers' combined 2026 capital expenditure What will the five major hyperscalers' combined capital expenditure be in calendar 2026? [40, 48, 114, 138, 223, 236, 254, 256, 267, 275, 344, 363]\nM03 False Five major hyperscalers' combined 2027 capital expenditure What will the five major hyperscalers' combined capital expenditure be in calendar 2027? [40, 42, 48, 114, 138, 223, 236, 254, 256, 267, 344, 363]\nM04 False Four hyperscalers' combined 2026 capital expenditure What will Amazon, Alphabet, Microsoft and Meta spend in aggregate on capital expenditures in calendar 2026? [13, 167, 181, 190]\nM05 False Worldwide semiconductor sales in 2026 What will worldwide semiconductor sales be in calendar 2026? [285]\nM06 True NVIDIA FY2027 data-center revenue What is NVIDIA's data-center revenue in FY2027? [28, 177, 181, 285, 322, 344]\nM07 True NVIDIA FY2028 data-center revenue What will NVIDIA's data-center revenue be in FY2028? [181, 189, 203, 223, 232, 254, 259, 285, 289, 307, 312, 314, 317, 319, 321, 322]\nM08 False NVIDIA future investment commitments at FY2027 year-end How much are NVIDIA's outstanding future investment commitments at FY2027 year-end? [118]\nM09 True NVIDIA FY2027 data-center networking revenue What is NVIDIA's data-center networking revenue in FY2027? [11]\nM10 True NVIDIA FY2028 non-GAAP gross margin What will NVIDIA's non-GAAP gross margin be in FY2028? [36, 40, 59, 108, 160, 181, 247, 256, 285, 307, 342]\nM11 True NVIDIA FY2028 total revenue What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2028? [9, 30, 36, 39, 40, 42, 48, 54, 56, 57, 58, 59, 66, 75, 81, 84, 87, 89, 91, 94, 108, 114, 118, 126, 128, 130, 132, 138, 145, 151, 160, 167, 340, 342, 346, 348, 349, 351, 354, 363, 366, 383, 387, 408, 410]\nM12 False NVIDIA OpenAI Ohio lease guarantee at FY2027 year-end What amount of NVIDIA's financial backstop for OpenAI's SB Energy Ohio data-center lease remains outstanding at FY2027 year-end? [9, 17, 118, 322]\nM13 False NVIDIA supply and capacity purchase commitments at FY2027 year-end How much will NVIDIA's outstanding supply and capacity purchase commitments total at the end of FY2027? [4, 94, 98, 104, 162, 232, 235, 254]\nM14 False Combined calendar-2027 capex of Amazon, Microsoft, Alphabet and Meta amid AI-slowdown debate What combined calendar-2027 capital expenditure will Amazon, Microsoft, Alphabet and Meta report, compared with 2026? [183, 191, 307, 323]\nM15 False Whether China formally permits imports of NVIDIA data center chips (H200) by 2027-01-31 Will China's government formally permit domestic companies to import NVIDIA H200/data center chips by 2027-01-31 (researcher-set check date: NVIDIA FY2027 year-end)? [75, 77, 384]\nM16 False Calendar