{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## D(190|197|505|671|676)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md | sed -n '7,37p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md | sed -n '100,128p'; rg -n --glob '*.py' 'served|practical|a - b' docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0 | head -52\"","aggregated_output":"2493:## D190 · 2026-10-26 · The collision judge: Jev for identity, the generative model for the analyst's question when a question may be held twice\n2551:## D197 · 2026-10-27 · A shared quantity is one thesis per theme, measure and period; its wording is not identity\n5835:## D505 · 2026-11-15 · Alex: the kept financial figures should reach the judgements of related questions; first a $0 check\n9589:## D671 · 2026-11-17 · Under D667 and D668 (council): the blind matter list is frozen at N = 32\n10007:## D676 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison: the new system loses for two known mechanisms; keep the old system; the outcome was computable before the run (council consensus)\n     7\t## The new system's mistakes, and the guard for each\n     8\t| Mistake | Where it showed | Guard in this plan |\n     9\t|---|---|---|\n    10\t| Steps were tuned on their own scores. The hand-off broke and was found at the end: Step 1's questions refused by the ladder, 19–27 of 60 (D432) | the release comparison, D676 | Every change is accepted only by its effect on final answers, read by blind readers on the analyst matter list. An end-to-end slice runs in week 1, not at the end |\n    11\t| The attainable verdict was not computed: $145 spent on a knowable result | D676 | The ceilings are below, computed before any send |\n    12\t| A policy removed matters by construction (company figures, D382), and it was known only at the end | D676 | Alex decides the figure questions for the hybrid now (below) |\n    13\t| Lines with no source, or that the change could not move (the merge test's P2) | D680 | Every line names its source and the change that can move it |\n    14\t| Choices made on the test set, and fix-and-rerun loops | council-loop traps | Designed on the stored failures of 09-07..09-20 (dev). Accepted once on a window the design never saw, with its matter list built blind before any hybrid output is read |\n    15\t\n    16\t## What the hybrid is\n    17\t| Piece | From | Status |\n    18\t|---|---|---|\n    19\t| Opening questions and their answer choices | Old (poc-v118) | Unchanged |\n    20\t| Reading articles | Old extraction (control arm) or clean Step 1 c8 (hybrid arm) | c8's effect on final answers is measured end to end, not assumed. On the 32 matters, old's losses are not reading losses |\n    21\t| Judging | Frozen judging-v7, then a new version (J2) | The change; Alex opened it on 2026-11-20 |\n    22\t| Clean Steps 2–3 | Not in the first build | Added only if a measured loss calls for them |\n    23\t\n    24\t## Attainable, on the frozen 32 matters (from the stored readings, $0)\n    25\t- **Old serves 10.**\n    26\t- **The judge fix can add M08 and M14.** Old opened each in 3 of 3 draws, and the readers rejected every answer for reasoning:\n    27\t  - adding amounts that overlap;\n    28\t  - a cumulative estimate taken for an outstanding balance;\n    29\t  - a five-company or company-forecast figure taken for a four-company answer.\n    30\t- **M30 (+1)** only if company figures are kept.\n    31\t- **M05, M09 and M25** (served in 1 of 3 draws) and the **17 never opened** move only with opening, not the judge.\n    32\t- **The release lead** (D665: a − b ≥ 5 and a ≥ 2b against old) is out of reach for the judge fix alone, with a ≤ 3. The judge fix is a\n    33\t  quality gain. A release needs phase 2, opening.\n    34\t- **If D382 applies to the hybrid** (no company-figure questions), old keeps 5–6 matters the hybrid cannot serve, and the hybrid loses by\n    35\t  construction. Hence Alex's decision now.\n    36\t\n    37\t## Phase 1: the judge (J2)\n   100\t  - Steps 2–3 grouping;\n   101\t  - the other 30 matters;\n   102\t  - cost.\n   103\t- **Cost, priced from tokens.** The merge pays the old pipeline plus c8 reading: about $0.0125 per article at $1.75 / 140. Over the\n   104\t  82-day window's 1,884 articles that is about $24 on top of old's about $9.\n   105\t- **The sampler-sensitive v47 question needs more than one draw** before stability is claimed.\n   106\t\n   107\t## Where the old system loses on the 32 matters, and why this merge cannot raise its score ($0, read after the verdict)\n   108\tSources: the comparison's `reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/mapping.json` and `deck/readings.json`, and the deck key.\n   109\t- **Old serves 10 and never opens 17.** The 17 are M01–M03, M07, M12, M16, M20–M24, M26–M29 and M32 (only new-3 opened M32). The merge\n   110\t  keeps old's opening, so these stay lost.\n   111\t- **Opened in at least 2 of 3 old draws but not served: M08, M14 and M30.**\n   112\t  - Every M08 and M14 answer was rejected by the readers. The readers' reasons are judge reasoning, not missing material:\n   113\t    - M14 (four companies' 2027 capex): rung 4 was taken from NVIDIA's own $1.3T forecast or a five-company $1.08T total. In old-1 the\n   114\t      material held BofA's four-company $930–980B.\n   115\t    - M08 (NVIDIA's outstanding investment commitments): $25B and $18B were added, though they probably overlap (old-2, old-3). In\n   116\t      old-1 the answer was anchored on Bank of America's $70B, a cumulative investment estimate rather than an outstanding balance.\n   117\t      (Corrected 2026-11-20. A first version cited \"a range against its own estimate of about $53B\". That card, C140, was a planted\n   118\t      reader control, not a system answer.)\n   119\t  - M30 is a company figure (D382/D505).\n   120\t- **Served in only 1 of 3 old draws:** M05, M09 and M25.\n   121\t- **The consequence.** Clean Step 1 reads more of the facts. The old system loses at opening and at the judge's reasoning, neither of\n   122\t  which better reading fixes. The test's targets, M04 and M17, were matters old already served, so the test could show \"does not\n   123\t  break\", never \"improves\". That was a design error of mine.\n   124\t- **Across all old cards rated worth tracking:** 18–21 of 28–29 supported per draw; 3–5 unsupported per draw.\n   125\t\n   126\t## Errors of mine in this test (logged)\n   127\t- **I read the census article numbers as positions in `kept-articles.json`.** They are numbers in `census/numbering.json`. Codex caught it\n   128\t  in round c. My first claim, that old filed none of the census articles, was wrong: 8 of 11 reached the old questions.\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/slice_checks.py:46:    reserved = trace.execute('select count(*) from trace').fetchone()[0]\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/slice_checks.py:48:    per_article_s = (t1 - t0).total_seconds() / max(1, reserved)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/slice_checks.py:49:    per_article_usd = (calls[0] or 0) / max(1, reserved)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/slice_checks.py:51:           {'articles': reserved, 'seconds per article': round(per_article_s, 1), 'usd per article (archive cost)': round(per_article_usd, 4)})\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/eligibility.py:73:    settled charges summing to the spend, nothing still reserved), since the ledger writes its log line after its own state.\"\"\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/eligibility.py:80:    if len(lines) != ledger['attempts'] + ledger['refused'] or abs(charged - ledger['spent']) > 1e-6 or ledger['reserved'] > 1e-9:\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/eligibility.py:82:                                  f\"{ledger['refused']} refusals, ${ledger['spent']:.6f} spent and ${ledger['reserved']:.6f} reserved\")\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_eligibility.py:32:        (root / 'ledgers' / f'{draw}.json').write_text(json.dumps({'attempts': 1, 'refused': 0, 'spent': 0.01, 'reserved': 0.0}))\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:60:def served_by(readings, counting):\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:61:    \"\"\"{system: set of matters served in at least 2 of its 3 draws} under one counting ('1': new favoured, '2': old favoured).\"\"\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:63:    served_draws = {}\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:78:                    served_draws.setdefault((system, matter), set()).add(draw)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:80:    return {s: {m for (sys_, m), draws in served_draws.items() if sys_ == s and len(draws) >= 2} for s in SYSTEMS}\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:121:    return {c: {'N': len(figure), 'a': len((set(v['served_new']) - set(v['served_old'])) & figure),\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:122:                'b': len((set(v['served_old']) - set(v['served_new'])) & figure)} for c, v in per_counting.items()}\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:497:            served = served_by(readings, counting)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:498:            a = len(served['new'] - served['old'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:499:            b = len(served['old'] - served['new'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:500:            per_counting[counting] = {'a': a, 'b': b, 'served_new': sorted(served['new']), 'served_old': sorted(served['old']),\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:525:        return dict(report, verdict='practical lead')\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:529:        return dict(report, verdict='practical loss', why=(['served matters'] if loss_count else []) + [f'guardrail {k}' for k in sorted(breaches)])\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:530:    return dict(report, verdict='no practical winner')\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mutants_reading_tools.py:24:     ['test_a_practical_lead_needs_the_margin_twice_b_and_every_guardrail_exercised_and_passing']),\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:25:def base(n=20, new_served=0, old_served=0, guard_cards=12):\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:26:    \"\"\"N matters; the first `new_served` served by the new system in all draws, the next `old_served` by the old one; every draw has\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:34:            served = (system == 'new' and i < new_served) or (system == 'old' and new_served <= i < new_served + old_served)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:35:            if served:\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:78:    r = base(new_served=10)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:85:    r = base(new_served=10)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:88:    r = base(new_served=10)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:95:    assert verdict(base(n=19, new_served=10))['verdict'] == 'too small'\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:96:    r = base(new_served=10)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:101:def test_a_practical_lead_needs_the_margin_twice_b_and_every_guardrail_exercised_and_passing():\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:102:    \"\"\"Rule: lead when a - b >= max(3, ceil(0.15 N)) and a >= 2b under both countings, with every guardrail exercised and passing.\"\"\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:103:    r = base(n=20, new_served=5, old_served=1)               # a 5, b 1: margin max(3, 3) = 3; 5 - 1 = 4 >= 3; 5 >= 2\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:104:    assert verdict(r)['verdict'] == 'practical lead'\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:105:    r = base(n=20, new_served=4, old_served=2)               # a 4, b 2: 4 - 2 = 2 < 3\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:106:    assert verdict(r)['verdict'] == 'no practical winner'\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:111:    assert verdict(base(n=20, new_served=5, old_served=1, guard_cards=3))['verdict'] == 'no practical winner'\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:112:    assert verdict(base(n=20, new_served=1, old_served=5, guard_cards=3))['verdict'] == 'practical loss'\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:117:    r = base(n=20, new_served=5, old_served=1)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:122:    assert out['verdict'] == 'practical loss' and 'guardrail figure' in out['why']\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:125:def test_a_matter_counts_as_served_only_in_two_of_three_draws():\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:126:    \"\"\"Rule: served by a system when served in at least 2 of its 3 draws.\"\"\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:127:    r = base(n=20, new_served=5, old_served=1)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:129:        r['mapping'][d].pop('M01')                             # M01 served by the new system in one draw only\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:136:    r = base(n=20, new_served=5, old_served=1)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:142:    assert out['verdict'] == 'practical lead'                 # 4 - 1 = 3 >= 3 and 4 >= 2 under counting 2 as well\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:147:    r = base(n=20, new_served=5, old_served=1)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:156:    r = base(n=20, new_served=5, old_served=1, guard_cards=10)          # 30 decided figure cards per system\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:163:    assert verdict(r)['verdict'] == 'practical lead'\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py:166:    assert out['verdict'] == 'practical loss' and 'guardrail figure' in out['why']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
