oc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-codex.txt:24:{\"matter\":\"M24\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"Q21 covers two neoclouds, not the five hyperscalers.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-codex.txt:26:{\"matter\":\"M26\",\"status\":\"broader\",\"ids\":[\"Q32\"],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"Acquisition completion encompasses required clearance, but Q32 does not measure the EU review stage at January 31, 2027.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-codex.txt:27:{\"matter\":\"M27\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"Q32 asks about completion, not the outstanding acquisition obligation amount at FY2027 year-end.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-codex.txt:28:{\"matter\":\"M28\",\"status\":\"broader\",\"ids\":[\"Q32\"],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"Acquisition completion encompasses required clearance, but Q32 does not measure the U.S. review stage at January 31, 2027.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-codex.txt:29:{\"matter\":\"M29\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"No Marvell FY2028 revenue question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-codex.txt:32:{\"matter\":\"M32\",\"status\":\"narrower\",\"ids\":[\"Q30\"],\"main_outcome\":true,\"note\":\"Q30 measures commitments to purchase unsold cloud capacity, covering a central component of neocloud capacity obligations.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:2:{\"matter\":\"M02\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"No question on five hyperscalers' combined 2026 capital expenditure.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:3:{\"matter\":\"M03\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"No question on five hyperscalers' combined 2027 capital expenditure.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:7:{\"matter\":\"M07\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"No question on NVIDIA FY2028 data-center revenue.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:12:{\"matter\":\"M12\",\"status\":\"broader\",\"ids\":[\"Q23\",\"Q26\"],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"OpenAI contractual commitments and aggregate lease credit support are wider categories that may include the Ohio guarantee.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:16:{\"matter\":\"M16\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"No question on 2027 DRAM contract prices.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:20:{\"matter\":\"M20\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"Q26 asks for outstanding aggregate support, not whether these particular agreements are signed.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:24:{\"matter\":\"M24\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"No question on five hyperscalers' combined 2026 data-center capital expenditure.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:26:{\"matter\":\"M26\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"No question on EU review of the Hugging Face acquisition.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:27:{\"matter\":\"M27\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"No question on the outstanding Hugging Face acquisition obligation.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:28:{\"matter\":\"M28\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"No question on U.S. review of the Hugging Face acquisition.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:29:{\"matter\":\"M29\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"No question on Marvell FY2028 revenue.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt:32:{\"matter\":\"M32\",\"status\":\"broader\",\"ids\":[\"Q6\"],\"main_outcome\":null,\"note\":\"Q6 asks about total supply and purchase commitments, rather than isolating neocloud capacity commitments.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:2:{\"matter\": \"M02\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No hyperscaler capex question; Q21 covers only the CoreWeave and Nebius neoclouds.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:3:{\"matter\": \"M03\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No 2027 hyperscaler capex question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:7:{\"matter\": \"M07\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No FY2028 data-center revenue question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:12:{\"matter\": \"M12\", \"status\": \"narrower\", \"ids\": [\"Q13\"], \"main_outcome\": false, \"note\": \"Q13 asks whether an Ohio guarantee is signed by 2027-12-31, not the amount outstanding at FY2027 year-end.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:16:{\"matter\": \"M16\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No DRAM price question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:20:{\"matter\": \"M20\", \"status\": \"opened\", \"ids\": [\"Q20\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Q20 asks whether the financing arrangement with Blackstone and others is signed by end-2027; it names Apollo rather than Goldman and does not mention residual-value support. Match is uncertain\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:24:{\"matter\": \"M24\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Q21 covers only the neoclouds, not hyperscalers.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:26:{\"matter\": \"M26\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No question on the stage of EU review of Hugging Face.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:27:{\"matter\": \"M27\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No question on the outstanding Hugging Face obligation amount.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:28:{\"matter\": \"M28\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No question on the stage of US antitrust review of Hugging Face.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:29:{\"matter\": \"M29\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No Marvell question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:32:{\"matter\": \"M32\", \"status\": \"opened\", \"ids\": [\"Q30\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Same 10-K figure for cloud-service capacity commitments to AI cloud partners at FY2027 year-end.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:2:{\"matter\": \"M02\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No hyperscaler capex question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:3:{\"matter\": \"M03\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No hyperscaler capex question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:7:{\"matter\": \"M07\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No NVIDIA data-center revenue question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:12:{\"matter\": \"M12\", \"status\": \"broader\", \"ids\": [\"Q26\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"The Ohio lease backstop is folded into Q26's aggregate of residual value guaranties and data-center lease credit support.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:16:{\"matter\": \"M16\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No DRAM pricing question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:20:{\"matter\": \"M20\", \"status\": \"broader\", \"ids\": [\"Q26\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Q26 measures aggregate residual value guaranties at FY2027 year-end; it reflects signing only indirectly, with a different date and shape.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:24:{\"matter\": \"M24\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No hyperscaler data-center capex question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:26:{\"matter\": \"M26\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No Hugging Face EU review question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:27:{\"matter\": \"M27\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No Hugging Face obligation question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:28:{\"matter\": \"M28\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No Hugging Face US antitrust question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:29:{\"matter\": \"M29\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No Marvell question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:32:{\"matter\": \"M32\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No question on cloud-service/neocloud capacity commitments. Q6 covers supply purchases, and Q1's credit support may only partly touch the backstops.\"}\n186:   \"matter\": \"M07\",\n358:   \"matter\": \"M12\",\n574:   \"matter\": \"M20\",\n722:   \"matter\": \"M27\",\n838:   \"matter\": \"M32\",\n830:  \"matter\": \"M07\",\n1522:  \"matter\": \"M12\",\n2363:  \"matter\": \"M20\",\n2810:  \"matter\": \"M27\",\n3191:  \"matter\": \"M32\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '2493,2505p;2551,2555p;5835,5846p;10021,10040p'; python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib; u=json.loads(pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/universe.json\\\").read_text()); print([(x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"name\\\"]) for x in u[\\\"companies\\\"]]); print(next(x for x in u[\\\"themes\\\"] if x[\\\"id\\\"]==\\\"semiconductor-cycle\\\"))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '2493,2505p;2551,2555p;5835,5846p;10021,10040p'; python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib; u=json.loads(pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/universe.json\\\").read_text()); print([(x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"name\\\"]) for x in u[\\\"companies\\\"]]); print(next(x for x in u[\\\"themes\\\"] if x[\\\"id\\\"]==\\\"semiconductor-cycle\\\"))'\"","aggregated_output":"  2493\t## D190 · 2026-10-26 · The collision judge: Jev for identity, the generative model for the analyst's question when a question may be held twice\n  2494\t\n  2495\t- Alex: \"查重是用的 Jev 吗？… 你可以先单独跑这个，重新 review 一次 Jev 的提示词，然后优化他，不仅达到你的目的，也更贴近 hedge fund analyst 的大脑，你有黄金集做标准\". Jev answers every candidate-to-thesis relation and every evidence comparison since D169.\n  2496\t- Review of Jev's relation criteria against the r3 ledger ([probe](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-admission-v12/jev-relation-probe/probe.md), 31 stored candidate calls whose list holds a thesis of the same object and measure, 18 labelled by the assistant): under the current options Jev calls a population variant of one aggregate `part_of` (0.4–0.9) and the code maps that to \"new\"; under an analyst's option set (\"one question: the same outcome settles both; another estimate, population or proxy of one aggregate is the same question\") it answers `distinct_question_same_matter` 0.5–0.9 on the same pairs. Both wordings: 8 of 18 right. Jev compares wording; it does not hold the decision. No change to Jev's criteria is made: the measured criteria stay (D167–D169).\n  2497\t- The generative model asked the same analyst question on the same 18 ([records](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-admission-v12/jev-relation-probe/llm-records.json), 3 samples each, $0.02): 11 of 18 right by majority, and 5 of the 6 aggregate duplicates merged; the misses are the debatable pairs (a reporting segment beside the business segment, the same deal under two names).\n  2498\t- Decided to build and run alone: `matching` keeps Jev; a configuration may add a `collision` setting (model, prompt `collision-v1`). When a candidate's list holds a thesis of its own object and measure, one generative call answers the analyst question for those theses and its verdict replaces Jev's on them (`jev_matching.collision_peers`, `ask_collision_judge`); every other relation stays Jev's. `poc-v26` = `poc-v25` plus the judge. Measured by one run over seed, week and August against the extraction gold and the census (ledger `english-v26-collision-r4-2026-10-26`); result appended here.\n  2499\t- General, not a list: the routing rule is a structural fact of the library (two theses of one object and quantity), and the question is the one a desk asks. The cost is one call per collision (31 of 69 candidates on r3), about $0.002 each.\n  2500\t- Result (run r4, `poc-v26`, seed + week + August, $1.33): 26 collision verdicts, 9 merges or successions, all on aggregate variants; 2026 aggregate theses 6 → 2 (v23: 11); theses 60 → 45; no merge removed a thesis the gold wants and A17 (the four-company figure as evidence to the five-company aggregate) turns full. The gold's overall score moved 9 → 4 full, and every lost case is an extraction difference between two fresh runs of the same v12 prompt (Rubin not opened from the call this time, the NAVER and META lines not extracted), not a matching decision. Recorded as the measurement rule for later arms: a matching change is judged on stored candidates and the duplicate census; an extraction change needs three fresh runs or pinned extraction answers; a one-run gold score carries about ±5 cases of sampler noise on this corpus. `poc-v25` stays the replay default until the judge is measured that way.\n  2501\t- Confirmation with extraction pinned (same recorded extraction answers in both arms, ids translated, Jev live, judging synthetic; `pinned_matching_study.py`): control reproduces r3 (60 theses, gold 9 full); the judge arm 56 theses, 2026 aggregates 6 → 3, evidence equal (711 vs 707 rows), gold 8 full with the one difference a repeat the scorer cannot see; 31 verdicts, 6 merges, $0.011; no required thesis lost. Alex: \"有效果我们可以做\". `poc-v26` becomes the replay default; `poc-v25` stays as a configuration. Open: the judge leaves 2 of 5 aggregate duplicates apart on one sample; a majority of three samples on collisions would cost three cents a run.\n  2502\t\n  2503\t## D191 · 2026-10-26 · Theme theses reach every company; no named dependant is required to open one\n  2504\t\n  2505\t- On the theme-dependency design (`docs/research/2026-10-26-theme-dependencies/design.md`), Alex decided the four points:\n  2551\t## D197 · 2026-10-27 · A shared quantity is one thesis per theme, measure and period; its wording is not identity\n  2552\t\n  2553\t- Alex: \"先把合计资本开支的重复主题题解决掉; 你小范围验证就好这个问题不要全部重跑，你能不能快速收敛\".\n  2554\t- The class ($0, `docs/research/2026-10-27-shared-quantity/proof.py`): every AI-capex aggregate candidate of r3, r4 and r5 (9, 11, 11) against the theses that existed before it. r3 (no collision judge) opened six 2026 aggregates; r4 and r5, with the judge, each opened one duplicate: the judge read \"Big Tech AI outlays\" against \"the top five's total capex\" (r4 seq 351) and \"the five named companies' capex\" against \"industrywide AI infrastructure spending\" (r5 seq 200) as distinct questions in one matter, and later candidates then merged into the duplicate (r4: two). The contract already says what identity is: `industry_aggregate` is \"one aggregate quantity for one calendar year … another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis\" (role-v12), and D155 puts identity in code where it is fully determined.\n  2555\t- Decided: a candidate admitted as `industry_aggregate` / `shared_quantity` with a quantity measure is keyed by (theme, measure, period) with no scope (`identity.automatic_key`); the writer records its key with `scope_source = 'shared'`; on the Jev path code decides its destination before any judge (`jev_matching.shared_quantity_target`): the open thesis of the same key is the same thesis (merge), the latest earlier period without a successor is its predecessor (succession), otherwise new. Policy stages and other events keep their event-typed identity; a company's own line (MSFT capex) is another object and never the aggregate; a theme quantity without the admission reason (the pre-D184 financing-amount case of T4) stays the model's. Tests: `tests/test_shared_quantity.py` (3, red first), suite 187.\n  5835\t## D505 · 2026-11-15 · Alex: the kept financial figures should reach the judgements of related questions; first a $0 check\n  5836\t\n  5837\t- **Asked** (after D504, his reply to this exact question, several answers allowed): \"对公司的主要财务数字（营收、毛利率的指引、市场预期、实际业绩），新系统已经存下来了，但现在既不展示也不判断。\n  5838\t  你希望读者能用它们做什么？（可多选）\" Options: reach the judgements of related questions (recommended); be looked up in a table; tracked questions\n  5839\t  with judgements; none for now.\n  5840\t- **Alex:** \"进入相关问题的判断 (Recommended)\" (the only option he chose). The option as shown: \"符合你定的规则：财务数字是观点的证据，不单独开成问题。第一步不花钱（$0）：检查现有问题做\n  5841\t  判断时，有没有系统存了、本该用到、却没送进去的财务数字。有就报给你，没有就停。\"\n  5842\t- **Decided:** the company's kept financial figures are evidence for the judgements of related questions; they are not opened as\n  5843\t  questions of their own (D382 and D384 stand), and he did not choose the table or tracked financial questions. The first step is a\n  5844\t  $0 check on the stored fresh-week run of the new system: for each existing question's judgement, is a kept financial figure it\n  5845\t  should have received absent from its request. A finding is reported to him; none ends the line. Nothing is sent to a model;\n  5846\t  nothing changes in the system by this check.\n 10021\t    - No new question was mapped out wrongly.\n 10022\t    - Codex found the old system's Anthropic serve generous; without it b is 6 or 7, still a loss.\n 10023\t  - **Mechanism 1, by design (D382, D384, D505):** the company's own figures are not questions. 7 of the 32 matters are such figures,\n 10024\t    and the old system serves 4 to 6 of them. By D384, five other companies' standalone figures are also outside the new system's\n 10025\t    rules, so its ceiling is 20 of 32 matters.\n 10026\t  - **Mechanism 2, a hand-off defect known since D432:**\n 10027\t    - Step 1 opens bundled questions (two years, or several outcomes), and the frozen ladder refuses them. new-2 lost 27 of 60 and new-3\n 10028\t      19 of 60.\n 10029\t    - Among them are four-hyperscaler capex (M04) and the Anthropic investment (M17) in both runs, and Hugging Face (M19) in new-2.\n 10030\t    - The judge uses pass 1's ladders; new-3's capex question got a valid ladder only on pass 3.\n 10031\t  - **The ceiling ($0 check):** with every dropped key-matter question repaired and served, new is 5–6 against old 10, a = 0, b = 4–5:\n 10032\t    no practical winner, never a lead. Only NVIDIA's own figures (M06, M10, M11, M18) remain.\n 10033\t  - **Process failure:** the attainable verdict was computable in minutes before the run, from the frozen list, D505, D432 and the D489\n 10034\t    week. Neither the council (D665–D667) nor Claude computed it (AGENTS §7.2); two days and about $145 measured a knowable result.\n 10035\t- **Decided (council consensus):**\n 10036\t  - The old system stays for release.\n 10037\t  - No further comparison run.\n 10038\t  - The new path continues only on Alex's word, and only after two things: his D382 call for such a comparison, and a cents-level test\n 10039\t    of the one-outcome hand-off repair on the stored no-ladder cases.\n 10040\t  - Before any future paid comparison, its attainable verdict is computed first.\n[('NVDA', 'NVIDIA'), ('TSM', 'Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing'), ('AMD', 'Advanced Micro Devices'), ('AVGO', 'Broadcom'), ('MU', 'Micron Technology'), ('INTC', 'Intel'), ('ASML', 'ASML Holding'), ('MSFT', 'Microsoft'), ('GOOGL', 'Alphabet'), ('AMZN', 'Amazon'), ('META', 'Meta Platforms'), ('ORCL', 'Oracle'), ('CRWV', 'CoreWeave'), ('SMCI', 'Super Micro Computer'), ('DELL', 'Dell Technologies')]\n{'id': 'semiconductor-cycle', 'name': 'Semiconductor cycle', 'categories': ['T1', 'T4', 'T6', 'T7', 'T8'], 'aliases': ['semiconductor cycle', 'semiconductor industry', '半导体周期', '半导体行业'], 'watch': [{'measure': 'growth_rate', 'scope': 'industry revenue', 'aliases': ['industry', 'semiconductor revenue', 'wsts', 'omdia']}], 'legacy_name': '半导体周期'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
